This appendix lists relevant learning and teaching standards, some of which directly concern CS, some of which concern social justice. Use this index to help identify chapters that cover particular standards, or to understand the scope of standards and the extent to which they engage social justice or CS.


# CSTA Learning Standards

The [CSTA learning standards|https://csteachers.org/pk12standards/] cover a broad set of CS concepts and skills. They were originally inspired by the [K-12 CS framework|http://k12cs.org], which broadly defined CS practices, concepts, and learning progressions for CS. These standards have been adopted widely across the United States as well as many other countries as foundational knowledge for primary and secondary learning, and were substantially revised in 2026. We include the secondary-level standards (middle school, high school, and high school specialties) here below. Where we propose a more critically conscious revision of a standard, the revised or added wording appears in *bold*; standards whose 2026 wording already weaves in critical, sociotechnical perspectives are shown unchanged.

